{
  "comment": "The hit-test contract (docs/mouse-positioning-spec.md MPOS-ARCH-2): every implementation runs these cases. TypeScript: app-native/shared/drag-snap/hit-test.test.ts; Rust: cli/crates/winctl/src/drag.rs (tests). A step is a pointer sample, a tick (a pause may be over) or the release; 'expect' is the transition ('none': the armed zone stays; null: disarmed) or, for a release, the zone of the drop. flags: shift 1, ctrl 2, alt 4, meta 8. stickPx: an armed zone holds a pointer that left its trigger by at most that much (and is in no other zone).",
